# Simulation Demo: "The Kintsugi Correction"

> **Context**: Use this script on a slide titled **"The Simulation Lab"**.
> **Scenario**: An RCM Orchestrator is negotiating a claim denial with an AI Payer Agent.
> **Format**: Chat Interface Transcript.

---

**[SYSTEM]:** Simulation #RC-402 Started. Topic: *Evaluation & Management (E&M) with Procedure*.
**[SCENE]:** You are billing for a Patient Visit (99213) + a Minor Surgery (10060) on the same day.
**[PAYER AGENT]:** "Claim denied. You cannot bill an Office Visit and a Surgery on the same day. It is unbundled."

---

**[STUDENT]:** "Okay, I will remove the Office Visit code (99213) and just bill the surgery."

---

**[THE MAESTRO - INTERVENTION]** ⏸️ *Simulation Paused*
> *Visual: The Student's text glows with a Golden Crack (Kintsugi Effect).*

**[MAESTRO]:** ⚠️ **Correction Opportunity**
You are about to lose **$120** in revenue.
**The Rule**: You *can* bill both if the visit was significant and separate from the surgery.
**The Fix**: You need **Modifier -25**.
**Try Again**: "I am appending Modifier -25 to the E&M code to indicate a significant, separate service."

---

**[STUDENT]:** *[Corrected Action]* "I am resubmitting the claim. I have added Modifier -25 to code 99213 to certify the visit was separate from the procedure."

---

**[PAYER AGENT]:** "Processing... Modifier -25 validated. Claim paid at 100% of allowable amount."

---

**[SYSTEM]:** ✅ **Simulation Complete.**
**Revenue Saved**: $120.00
**Compliance Score**: 100%
**Mastery Level**: Gold.
